---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Docs title="Runners">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-10">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Runners</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Connect Craig to your preferred AI agent CLI.</p>

    <p>
      Craig supports <strong>Claude Code</strong>, <strong>Codex</strong>, and <strong>Cursor</strong> as runner backends.
      Each runner must be installed and available in your <code>PATH</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Selecting a runner</h2>
    <p>When creating a task, Craig presents available runners. You can also specify one explicitly:</p>
    <pre><code>craig task new --runner claude "your task prompt"</code></pre>

    <h2>Enabling / disabling runners</h2>
    <p>Configure which runners are available in <code>.craig/config.json</code>:</p>
    <pre><code>{`{
  "runners": {
    "codex":  { "enabled": true },
    "cursor": { "enabled": true },
    "claude": { "enabled": false }
  }
}`}</code></pre>

    <h2>Custom runner path</h2>
    <p>
      If your runner binary isn't on your default <code>PATH</code>, override the path in config.
      Path changes apply to newly created task sessions.
    </p>
    <pre><code>{`{
  "runners": {
    "claude": {
      "enabled": true,
      "path": "/usr/local/bin/claude"
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>
  </div>
  </div>
</Docs>
